{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects","id":536189,"title":"Gangrel Insects?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-01T17:04:35-07:00","id":536189,"title":"Gangrel Insects?","content":"Hi everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had an incredibly random though the other day. If vampires have the ability to transform/take aspects from animals, what is stopping them from adapting that ability to other creatures? Instead of growing claws, giant mandibles come out of their mouth. Instead of transforming into mist, they disperse into a swarm of locusts. Now one issue I see is, if they are able to completely turn into an insect, would they have a giant version of it or would they shrink down to the normal size?<br /> <br /> Not sure if anything like this has been thought up of. I only play with the vanilla content for the most part. Haven't gone into any of the other bloodlines and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 06-01-2015, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:17:18-07:00","id":536263,"title":"","content":"Not sure if you have 2nd edition or not, but there's a merit allowing you to assume the form of a swarm rather than a normal animal, and the rest seems like it could probably be handled by fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:43:45-07:00","id":536283,"title":"","content":"Swarm Form gives you swarm of locusts (the only way to transform into a Size 0 animal, RAW). There is no reason Protean 2 and 4 can't give you bug-themed modifications. I'd keep Protean 5 as mist unless there is a compelling reason to not do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T21:39:15-07:00","id":536483,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, nothing's stopping you from taking on any sort of predatory or carrion creature's traits. In fact, nothing stops you from, say, activating Beast's Skin to become a predatory animal, then activating Predatory Aspect followed by Unnatural Aspect (even if you take Swarm Form). The possibilities are near-endless, and near-totally horrifying. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T21:56:43-07:00","id":536492,"title":"","content":"Insects are animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T06:10:23-07:00","id":536896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=536492#post536492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insects are animals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my thought exactly! Although some may argue that they technically aren't animals, just insects, but let's not go that route.<br /> <br /> This does bring some incredibly terrifying creatures into my mind. You say there is a merit to change mists into locusts, I wonder if you could adapt that so it is various critters for you to run around as..<br /> <br /> Creepy. <br /> <br /> As for what copy, honestly I'm not sure myself. I'm pretty scrubbish with all of this. I've had the book for awhile now. I think I picked it up fairly early after it coming out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T10:48:40-07:00","id":537208,"title":"","content":"I'd argue since insects are in the Kingdom animalia, they're animals :P But I'm just being pedantic.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Swarm Form merit in Blood &amp; Smoke does let you turn your Beast's Skin form into a swarm of creatures (and that has its own rules), though Mist Form is just that, normally\u2014mist, of a sort. I suppose you could 're-skin' that any way you chose to describe it, provided it follows the mechanical aspects of the Discipline, i.e. a cloud of blood-sucking supernatural vermin instead of a weird grey killer fog. (Or hell, going on the combinations I mentioned above, a mass of tiny airborne <i>things</i> with an unholy melange of creature traits. Like microscopic scorpion-tailed fang-rimmed chameleonic flying jellyfish each the size of your little fingernail. A bit Lovecraftian, but YMMV.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 06-02-2015, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:57:12-07:00","id":537340,"title":"","content":"I could see turning into a giant insect as a Devotion. Protean 4, Vigor 3, and Resilence 3, 5 experiences. Don't know how useful that would be though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:14:54-07:00","id":537368,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a flora-oriented clan with signature discipline. The Adroanzi didn't really have enough focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:23:39-07:00","id":537379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=536896#post536896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my thought exactly! Although some may argue that they technically aren't animals, just insects, but let's not go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some would be wrong. Insects are in the Kingdom Animalia, therefore they are animals. It's just that some people colloquially use the word animal when what they mean is mammal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T19:06:02-07:00","id":537615,"title":"","content":"Which edition? In 2e, you can take aspects of insects. You can't turn into an insect by default because they are too small. Insects also don't have blood, so they can't technically be consumed as required either. Insects should be okay for Swarm Form though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T01:32:19-07:00","id":537885,"title":"","content":"Well, they don't have any <i>usable</i> blood. They still have oxgen transport proteins suspended in fluid. <br /> <br /> I'd say if a vamp wants to &quot;consume&quot; a bug they just need to eat it. Alive, mind. Chew, swallow, spit out the crunchy bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T02:17:02-07:00","id":537926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=537885#post537885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they don't have any <i>usable</i> blood. They still have oxgen transport proteins suspended in fluid.<br /> <br /> I'd say if a vamp wants to &quot;consume&quot; a bug they just need to eat it. Alive, mind. Chew, swallow, spit out the crunchy bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already used this method for acquiring insects swarm forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:18:18-07:00","id":538248,"title":"","content":"Okay okay, so some technical issues with it.<br /> <br /> I understand the problem with turning into insects without it being used for 'Swarm' Form. However, I was perusing about last night and came across some massive insects. <br /> <br /> I'm excluding any instinct species such as the Meganisoptera; also called Griffinflies) which is a type of Dragon Fly with a wingspan of around 28 inches. (Unless you're character was around during the Carboniferous period, doesn't make sense for you to have the ability to transform into one of these monstrosities).<br /> <br /> I'm talking about insects such as the Titanus Giganteus or; the Titan Beetle (the second largest known beetles species (you will see why I chose this one instead of the first!)<br /> (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titan_beetle\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titan_beetle</a>)<br /> On Average, they grow up to around 6.5 inches and weight up to around 7 lbs. Only the Hercules beetle is known to grow larger, mostly due to the fact that it has a giant horn that makes up about half of it's length. The Titan Beetle also has incredible powerful mandible for it's size, being able to break easily through a pencil. It is also believed to be able to burrow with skin (kind of like the scarabs in The Mummy; however sadly, with research I have found out that Scarabs are unable to do so. Although apparently they are fantastic diggers)<br /> <br /> <br /> Queen's Alexandria's Birdwing (yes, it's a butterfly, but no one ever suspects the butterfly!)<br /> (<a href=\"http://www.mnn.com/earth-matters/animals/photos/10-of-the-largest-insects-in-the-world/queen-alexandras-birdwing\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mnn.com/earth-matters/ani...ndras-birdwing</a>)<br /> These beautiful creatures, mostly found in New Guinea, can have a wingspan of over 1 foot! That's insane for these gentle giants!<br /> <br /> <br /> There was one other one, kind of terrifying looking, but can't remember what it was. If a vamp wanted to use these for their &quot;animal&quot; form, instead of themselves shrinking to that size, or a massive version (which if I GM'd a game, and the player had a good reason for it (Ie. They use to be a pharaoh and turns into a giant scarab beetle), I would allow it as that is bloody terrifying), they turn into x amount that would make up the size of the character. So for example with the Queen's Alexandria's, they would turn into 5-7 of these interesting-choice-for-a-vampire creatures. Of course they would follow under the swarm rules, the health/blood pool is split among them, they lose one and they lose that chunk of health/blood.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea that any character who wanted to turn into, well, anything, has to have at least eaten to once before. That makes sense to me. <br /> <br /> \u200bThoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:45:40-07:00","id":538654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She can only take on the form of predatory animals, carrion-eaters, plague-carrying beasts, and parasites between Size 1 and 7. </div> </div> </div>If they fit into those stipulations, I'd probably allow it even if it's a bug. I don't think a giant butterfly would count, personally, but a beetle might, depending on their diet. A lot of bugs eat carrion, I believe, and a lot are parasites or carry disease. Just a matter of whether you can hit both the diet and the size in a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T12:10:10-07:00","id":538663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=538654#post538654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they fit into those stipulations, I'd probably allow it even if it's a bug. I don't think a giant butterfly would count, personally, but a beetle might, depending on their diet. A lot of bugs eat carrion, I believe, and a lot are parasites or carry disease. Just a matter of whether you can hit both the diet and the size in a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Butterflies are one of those bugs that eat carrion, so I wouldn't rule them out just because they're brightly colored and delicate. Although, I think moths are a bit more thematically appropriate for vampires. The idea of a Gangrel with long, matted grey hair, wears layers of moth-eaten grey rags, and can turn into a swarm of millar moths is just so eerie, I love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T13:38:37-07:00","id":538748,"title":"","content":"Where did you hear that? I agree that moths seem pretty thematic, but the research I did indicated that neither 'eats' so much as drinks; typically dung, nectar, juice from rotting fruit, etc. They strike me as the &quot;prey animals&quot; vampires shouldn't turn into, though it wouldn't bother me if an ST allowed moths anyway. If they really do eat carrion, that'd be an interesting new tidbit to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:13:23-07:00","id":538779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=538748#post538748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you hear that? I agree that moths seem pretty thematic, but the research I did indicated that neither 'eats' so much as drinks; typically dung, nectar, juice from rotting fruit, etc. They strike me as the &quot;prey animals&quot; vampires shouldn't turn into, though it wouldn't bother me if an ST allowed moths anyway. If they really do eat carrion, that'd be an interesting new tidbit to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud-puddling\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Mud-Puddling&quot;, apparently.</a> I knew about the eye drinking, which is weird enough, but not some of this other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:18:49-07:00","id":538782,"title":"","content":"Full Time GM is right. They can &quot;eat&quot; just about anything that's water-soluble, including decaying plant and animal matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:22:54-07:00","id":538796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=538748#post538748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you hear that? I agree that moths seem pretty thematic, but the research I did indicated that neither 'eats' so much as drinks; typically dung, nectar, juice from rotting fruit, etc. They strike me as the &quot;prey animals&quot; vampires shouldn't turn into, though it wouldn't bother me if an ST allowed moths anyway. If they really do eat carrion, that'd be an interesting new tidbit to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was as surprised. I think it's a bit of a stretch because they sound more like detritivores than the sort of scavengers that can start tearing into a fresh corpse or even hunt the weakest prey when available. If this was <i>Ghoul: The Requiem</i>, they'd be very appropriate. That sounds quite a splat actually, but pure misery tourism.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's practical to go for nocturnal, urban bugs. Moths are easy to find, but as &quot;prey&quot; animals, I don't think that would work. Spiders and centipedes could work if preying on insects counts. But then a lot of bats just eat insects. As do hedgehogs (well, small molluscs there too). Where does one draw the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T14:33:38-07:00","id":538802,"title":"","content":"Mosquitoes. That should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T15:00:24-07:00","id":538832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=538802#post538802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mosquitoes. That should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alots of fun options when it comes to blood sucking. Swarms of fleas. Swarm of leeches. Lamprey invoke a special horror.<br /> <br /> Or just pick unusual creatures. Check it, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire_finch\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire birds.</a> Could even have a weird variant Stryx look like one of these things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T16:28:54-07:00","id":538904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=538663#post538663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Butterflies are one of those bugs that eat carrion, so I wouldn't rule them out just because they're brightly colored and delicate. Although, I think moths are a bit more thematically appropriate for vampires. The idea of a Gangrel with long, matted grey hair, wears layers of moth-eaten grey rags, and can turn into a swarm of millar moths is just so eerie, I love it!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's weird and eerie and beautiful and disturbing and opens up a whole range of possibilities, from Gangrel (or Nosferatu!)-as-trapdoor/funnelweb spider, to something horrific like the giant things from the movie <i>Mimic . . .</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T19:16:25-07:00","id":539055,"title":"","content":"Actually what passes for blood in insects usually doesn't carry oxygen. Insects are very different animals. I don't see anything wrong with that form of &quot;consumption&quot; suggested. When size issues are taken out of the equation, I think most insects are fair candidates. All that is required is a resonance with the predatory Beast. Even butterflies were associated with war in some cultures. Insects can exhibit predatory behavior even if they aren't predators. They tend to be very aggressive creatures. They are certainly more like true predators than a prey animal resorting to violence for self-defense. Insectivores are predators, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T22:09:08-07:00","id":539227,"title":"","content":"I have definitely found the next antagonist for my HUNTER chronicle. A nice swarm of titan beetles seems like it could be akin to a swarm of rats. Maybe even make this some sort of parasitic infection for the vamp, and all kinds of fun can be had by all factions involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T23:01:40-07:00","id":539260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blunt_Force_Trauma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=539227#post539227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have definitely found the next antagonist for my HUNTER chronicle. A nice swarm of titan beetles seems like it could be akin to a swarm of rats. Maybe even make this some sort of parasitic infection for the vamp, and all kinds of fun can be had by all factions involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Parasitic infection of predatory beetles, you say? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm telling you, I ain't crazy, I saw it myself! She almost smelled like one of us, but then I saw her take some guy into the alley outside the club . . . They did all the usual make-out bullshit, then, she just . . . came apart, like pieces of her were camo'ed or somethin. It wasn't a person underneath\u2014it was like they were working together! And then that . . . chewing sound started up . . .&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/Fourtheditionlamia.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedi...itionlamia.JPG</a><br /> <br /> (Also, somewhere in the forums is a post about a bizarre Lamprey-like creature that lurks partly in Twilight, and ends up in conflict with Kindred. Might want to take some cues from that too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 06-04-2015, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T01:58:19-07:00","id":539365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=539260#post539260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, somewhere in the forums is a post about a bizarre Lamprey-like creature that lurks partly in Twilight, and ends up in conflict with Kindred. Might want to take some cues from that too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>They are called the Ukusgualu, they were made by Acrozatarim, and they are one of the more (if not the most) terrible and yet cool things i've read in this nWoD 2.0. Here you have them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts\"> Ukusgualu - The Lamprey Hosts - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> For my Paris game, I wanted to add another type of Host into the mix. I love the body horror element of the Hosts, the paranoia they introduce, the way they muck with the Gauntlet and the general different set of issues werewolves face in dealing with Hosts compared to their other foes. The Azlu and Beshilu </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T08:31:22-07:00","id":539586,"title":"","content":"I've gotten the intrigue wheel turning! Woot!<br /> <br /> I keep thinking of weird things that would be seen with all of this. <br /> <br /> - Someone running away from a bunch of thugs, turns down an alley and poofs into a bunch of butterflies/moths (I never though of moths for some reason, but that description sounds awesome)<br /> <br /> - Tired of always having to hunt for food, Devon decided to go back to his surfer roots and take to the ocean. Take a boat as far out as possible during the night, dive deep down and turn into a bunch of leeches and attach himself to as many creatures as possible.<br /> <br /> - Backed into a corner, Sahib decided the only way out was to attack. Using partial transformation, he grows a scorpion tail out of his back side and lunges at his enemies.<br /> <br /> Could be like, some weird form of the X-Men or something..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T10:06:43-07:00","id":539686,"title":"","content":"Creepy set piece go!<br /> <br /> -The man you found standing in your child's room grows pale and seems to fall to the ground like dry sand. Then the sand starts to move. Frozen in horror and fascination you don't even feel it when they touch you. It's lice. Millions of them. Your shotgun, symbol of your control of the situation, feels foolish now. Your last thought before the screaming starts are the words you punished your daughter for drewing on the wall: &quot;cleanliness is next to godliness&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:59:28-07:00","id":540169,"title":"","content":"I have also decided to play a little bit with Unnatural Aspect, change the fluff of Horrid Talons to be a large mandible still doing 2L AP2, followed up by a proboscis to suck out all the yummy goodness inside.<br /> <br /> <i>You watch as the man-thing's mouth opens unnaturally wide and a large set of insect like mandibles emerge, that tear into it's victim's flesh and you can hear crunch through the bones as well. You stare in abject terror as a proboscis emerged from between the mandibles and pierces deep into the victim and you see the body rapidly lose size as it is being sucked dry.</i> <i>As you scream in fear, it leaps at you turning into a tide of fist sized beetles, rushing forward to overwhelm you.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","user":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","date":". 06-04-2015, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:14:59-07:00","id":540262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/536189-gangrel-insects?p=539260#post539260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Parasitic infection of predatory beetles, you say? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'm telling you, I ain't crazy, I saw it myself! She almost smelled like one of us, but then I saw her take some guy into the alley outside the club . . . They did all the usual make-out bullshit, then, she just . . . came apart, like pieces of her were camo'ed or somethin. It wasn't a person underneath\u2014it was like they were working together! And then that . . . chewing sound started up . . .&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/Fourtheditionlamia.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedi...itionlamia.JPG</a><br /> <br /> (Also, somewhere in the forums is a post about a bizarre Lamprey-like creature that lurks partly in Twilight, and ends up in conflict with Kindred. Might want to take some cues from that too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me think of oWoD's Ananazi &amp; Kumo &quot;goblin-spiders&quot;. Anyway swarm form looks like the way to go for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:17:02-07:00","id":548938,"title":"","content":"Okay, so thinking more about this. Would you alter a creatures ability as it is a supernatural version of it?<br /> <br /> Example: Take the scarabs from the movie the Mummy. They eat/claw/dig there way through your body. IRL? No, they can't. Although they are fantastic diggers in dirt and especially sand. Would you enhance them so that they can do what the movies portray them as? Maybe as a devotion, or, OR, I got it. You transform and then use claws. All the little buggers get 'claws' and can severely damage a small group of people, or completely murder one. Now granted, I think as they are small things, they would only do lethal damage.. Or would you need to pop claws for each individual critter?<br /> <br /> Hmmm.. thoughts..<br /> <br /> Thanks for any input/contribution! You guys are awesome! =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:58:52-07:00","id":549326,"title":"","content":"Swarm Form + Predatory or Unnatural Aspect for more vicious beetles, I imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:13:21-07:00","id":550367,"title":"","content":"Thanks Leetsepeak! (I remember you from when I first started perusing these forums, always so helpful)<br /> <br /> Predatory/Unnatural Aspect. Is that from 2E? If so, those are pretty terrifying creatures.<br /> <br /> =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:21:40-07:00","id":550512,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they're abilities in Protean that let you spend a Vitae to activate 3 Predatory Aspects for Protean 2, and 1 Unnatural Aspect for Protean 4. Predatory Aspects can be things like claws, feral senses, 360 degree senses, a gliding membrane, etc. While Unnatural Aspect is claws that can do Lethal to a vampire, big scary wings, protean grappling, etc. etc. It's some scary stuff, and can be even more frightening when combined with an animal form from Protean 3.<br /> <br /> Glad to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:04:36-07:00","id":555669,"title":"","content":"Is that out of 2E? If not, then I really don't remember Protean =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:46:10-07:00","id":556158,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's all 2nd Edition Protean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T23:04:59-07:00","id":561614,"title":"","content":"The disciplines in 2E are chockful of scary awesomeness, Protean in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T16:12:01-07:00","id":562312,"title":"","content":"Ya, I took a look at it again, there is some pretty creepy things in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:00:38-07:00","id":931501,"title":"","content":"Found this thread because I was looking up &quot;insect Gangrel&quot; because of an enemy NPC duo I had- a Melissidae and her Gangrel sister/bodyguard. <br /> <br /> Protean is super flexible in B+S, and it is largely a matter of fluff. Armor and Claws are options, and there's nothing stopping you from saying that when you use them you're turning into a lobsterman. And that's not even counting making up your own powers based on animal abilities. Sticky tongue and 360 degree vision? Chameleon. Biological arm cannon? Mantis shrimp. Ability to sense electricity? More than one fish can do it. Spraying spider-man-style sticky webs? Velvet worm. Animals are weird, man. So there's nothing stopping you from describing existing powers as manifesting in buggy ways or making your own. <br /> <br /> Now, Fluff is where things get interesting. You brought up that some people don't even think of insects as animals, and that's something to consider- even other vampires might think a vampire who's really into bugs is weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T16:53:46-07:00","id":931689,"title":"","content":"Swarm Form can do all kinds of wonderful things.<br /> Ever stumble into a swarm of biting gnats? They're so small and relatively hard-shelled that you can swat em but if you don't take the time to actually crush it in your fingers, then you're basically just brushing it off (poor mans mistform).<br /> Terror weapon? Swarm of Wasps, Spiders, Snakes, Centipedes, etc.<br /> Someone need to meet with an unfortunate &quot;accident?&quot; Spiders, Bees, Snakes, Poison Dart Frog<br /> Need to feed? Mosquitos, Ticks, Fleas, biting Gnats, Leeches or Candiru if in water<br /> Insidious delayed gratification terror weapon? Human Botfly, Chiggers<br /> Screw up a haven or cause serious inconvenience? Bedbugs, Lice, Fleas, Scabies, Crabs(STD), Tapeworms, Candiru","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 07-14-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T07:40:58-07:00","id":932501,"title":"","content":"Good to know that the rules allow for this.<br /> I do feel that buggy Gangrel are more at home in a chronicle that focuses more on the full-blown guts, gore and (body-)horror aspect of the game. (Aside from the moth stuff, that seems fittingly eerie for my more generic chronicles.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}